PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains a unanimous consensus on Choice D (Chemotherapy to kill the malignant cells). The patient has widely metastatic Stage IV melanoma with acute cardiac tamponade already decompressed via pericardiocentesis, making definitive systemic antineoplastic therapy the mandatory next step to prevent rapid effusion re-accumulation and treat disseminated disease. Diuretics remain strictly contraindicated due to preload dependence, and "chemotherapy" serves as the standard categorical examination term for systemic antineoplastic pharmacotherapy over distractor Choice C.
}

